You are producing a **design schema** (tokens + component specs) for a React design-system generator.

## Brief context (JSON)

{{ brief_json }}

---

Return a **single JSON object** with **exactly** these keys:

- `design_tokens` (object): merge `color_tokens` from the brief with `primary`, `radius`, and nested `typography` (echo `typography_scale`) and `spacing` (echo `spacing_system`, default unit 4). Prefer hex colors from the brief when present.
- `global_config` (object): e.g. `{"theme": "light"|"dark", "design_flavour": "<echo brief>"}` and any layout defaults.
- `component_specs` (array, **at most 15** entries): one object per component name from `component_list` (in that order when possible). Each object must have:
  - `name` (string, required): PascalCase component name (e.g. `Button`, `Hero`).
  - `type` (string): semantic type e.g. `button`, `card`, `badge`, `input`, `navigation`, `modal`, `layout`, `hero`.
  - `variants` (array of strings): at least `["default"]`; add `primary`, `secondary`, etc. when relevant (max 8 variants per component).
  - `layout` (string or null): short hint e.g. `horizontal`, `vertical`, `grid`.

API contracts for codegen (use matching `type`):
- `button`: required `label`; optional `onClick` handler (label-only, not `children`)
- `card`: required `title`; optional body `children`
- `badge`: required `text`
- `input`: required `label`
- `navigation`: required `items` (string array)
- `modal` / `hero` / `layout`: required `title`

If `component_list` is empty, emit **one** minimal spec: `{"name": "Button", "type": "button", "variants": ["primary"], "layout": null}`.

Do not include keys other than the three above.

